doc:
player_title: shows a title and a subtitle (text rules and packed `args` of basalt_player_send, one block for both;
empty subtitle for none) with the timings in ticks. OK; INVALID for a negative timing; ABSENT for a missing lang key;
STALE.

recipe_station: what a crafting station makes, as a value (needed-length). `kind` and `input`:
  "crafting"   input {"width": int, "height": int, "items": list of item values or null, row by row}
               answer {"recipe": string, "result": item, "remaining": list of item or null}
  "anvil"      input {"left": item or null, "right": item or null, "name": string optional}
               answer {"result": item or null, "cost": int, "materials": int}
  "smithing"   input {"template": item or null, "base": item or null, "addition": item or null}
               answer {"recipe": string, "result": item}
ABSENT when no recipe fits, INVALID for an unknown kind or a bad input.

profile_lookup: looks a player name up on Mojang's services without stopping the server. Returns a request handle;
later basalt_callback(token, ctx) runs with a completion ctx whose value_result is {uuid, name, texture, signature}
or null when the name is unknown or the services are unreachable (texture and signature are empty when the account
has none; with them the value is about 2 KB, so read it into a 4 KB buffer). request_cancel drops it. INVALID for an empty name or too many pending requests.

task_at: calls basalt_callback(token, ctx) once the server runs the code that owns the place (the region of a world
position), with a completion ctx whose value_result is null. The world is a name. Returns a request handle;
ABSENT for an unknown world, INVALID for an empty one.

noise_query: evaluates terrain data for a seed without generating a chunk. `spec` is a map {op, settings
(`minecraft:overworld`), seed (i64), ...}. ops: shape (answers {min_y, height, sea_level, default_block,
default_fluid, legacy_random_source, disable_mob_generation}); density (function: `final_density`, `continents`,
`erosion`, `depth`, `ridges`, `temperature`, `vegetation`; x, y, z; answers a float); density_tree (json, x, y, z);
noise (id, x, y, z as floats); noise_range (id; answers [min, max]); height (x, z, ocean_floor?; answers an int);
column (x, z; answers bytes of i32 state ids, bottom first). ABSENT when the settings, function or noise are unknown.
